<title>BELGIUM: Belcofi 1996 profit up 7.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Belcofi 1996 profit up 7.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996</p>
<p>(In millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit				807   vs     749.8</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)			  43   vs	40</p>
<p>    Group net profit per share (francs)     198   vs     184</p>
<p>NOTE - Belcofi, owned 55.1 percent by another Belgian holding company, Ackermans &amp; van Haaren (AvH), said that earnings were influenced by the reshuffle in June 1996 of the group structure of previously state-owned holding company NIM/SNI by Belcofi and AvH.  </p>
<p>    Goodwill depreciation		     1,654  vs	359.7</p>
<p>    Group own funds			     8,465  vs    9,419.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Under the reshuffle, Belcofi sold its 50 percent stake in NIM/SNI to AvH but acquired NIM's 63.72 stake in development capital portfolio holder Sofinim.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
